# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MLO WANGU Mobile — Environment Variables (names only, never commit actual values)
# Copy to .env and fill in real values before running.
# .env is gitignored (see the repo root .gitignore's `.env*` rule). Never commit it.
#
# IMPORTANT: every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable is bundled into the client and is
# readable by anyone who has the app. Only put values here that are safe to be
# public. Never put a service-role key, admin credential, or any server-only
# secret in this file — those stay in the root .env, used only by server.ts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Same Supabase project the web app already uses — Settings → API in the
# Supabase dashboard. The anon key is designed to be public; Row Level
# Security (not secrecy of this key) is what protects data. Used here ONLY
# for Supabase Auth calls (sign-in/refresh/sign-out) — the app never queries
# a Supabase table directly with this key; all application data goes through
# the Express API below.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=...
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...

# The existing Express API's base URL.
# - iOS Simulator: http://localhost:3000
# - Android Emulator: http://10.0.2.2:3000  (localhost on the host machine)
# - Physical device (Expo Go / dev build) on the same Wi-Fi: http://<your-machine-LAN-IP>:3000
# - Production: your deployed server's HTTPS URL
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
